---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Elixir Community collects, why, and your rights."
>
  <div class="container-page">
    <PageHeader title="Privacy" />
    <article class="typography mt-12 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-(--ec-muted)">Updated 7 October 2026</p>
      <p>
        This page explains what we collect when you sign up for the newsletter
        or use this site, and what we do with it. In short: we only need your
        email address, we only use it to send the newsletter, and you can leave
        at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Elixir Community is run by Tomasz Tomczyk, who is the controller of
        newsletter personal data. Questions about your data go to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@elixir.community">hello@elixir.community</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What we collect:</strong> your email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Why:</strong> to send you the newsletter. Our legal basis
          under UK GDPR is your consent.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Double opt-in:</strong> after you sign up, we send a
          confirmation email. You get no newsletter until you confirm.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Leaving:</strong> every email has an unsubscribe link. Using
          it withdraws your consent.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where your email is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Your email address, contact record and consent status are kept in{' '}
        <a href="https://www.useplunk.com/privacy">Plunk</a>, which also sends
        our emails.
      </p>
      <p>
        Plunk tracks when our newsletter emails are opened and when links in
        them are clicked.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your contact while you are subscribed, and after that only as
        long as needed to respect your unsubscribe. If you never confirm, your
        pending contact may stay in Plunk until we remove it by hand. You can
        ask us to delete your data at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Confirmation links</h2>
      <p>
        Confirmation links work for 24 hours. Pressing Confirm in that time
        subscribes the address the link was sent to, even if it was unsubscribed
        in between. Links stop working once we delete a contact.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare hosts the site. We use it for three things, none of which set
        cookies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Visitor statistics:</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics gives us
          totals for visits, page views and performance.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bot protection:</strong> Cloudflare Turnstile checks
          newsletter signups for bots and abuse. To do that it looks at
          technical details of your browser and network. See Cloudflare's{' '}
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/turnstile-privacy-policy/">
            Turnstile privacy addendum
          </a>
          .
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Link clicks:</strong> when you click a link to another site,
          we count it. We store the link address (without its query string), the
          page you were on and the time, for three months. Nothing that
          identifies you is stored.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Outside the UK</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare and Plunk process data for us, and some of it happens outside
        the UK and EEA. Cloudflare runs a global network. Plunk stores data in
        the EEA and sends email through Amazon SES, which can process data in
        other countries. See the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a> and{' '}
        <a href="https://www.useplunk.com/privacy">Plunk</a> privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          give you a copy of your data, or send it to you in a portable format
        </li>
        <li>correct it</li>
        <li>delete it</li>
        <li>limit how we use it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of these rights only apply in certain cases. You can also withdraw
        your consent at any time. To do any of this, email{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@elixir.community">hello@elixir.community</a>. If
        you are unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">
          Information Commissioner's Office
        </a>
        .
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If what we collect changes, we will update this page and the date at the
        top.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
